**The per-entry timeout and the total scan budget use the same value.**

`qw_scan_registry_jobs` receives `$scan_timeout` as the budget for one registry entry. The subprocesses run in sequence. The worst-case total runtime is therefore `(count($sovereign_sites) + count($isolated_networks)) * $scan_timeout`.

The parent worker applies the same value as the budget for the entire scan. In `src/class-worker-process.php` line 1045, `poll_full_rescan` terminates the scan when `time() - $scan['started'] > $this->scan_timeout`. With two or more slow registry entries, the parent kills the scanner before it prints any output, and every job found so far is discarded.

Derive a per-entry budget from the remaining total time instead of reusing the full value.



